A Loom AIE2P setup fix for images of other layouts sharing a context (LOOM_EXP_ROUTE_RESET; yah gen_npu_gemm ghelp
images next to images without it):
- A core reset does not withdraw an acquire the core was stalled in. The request stays pending in the lock's module
  and takes the first token that lock gets under the next image. Seen: the gate relay, parked on its west neighbor's
  handoff lock, was reset by the next image's setup, where that lock id is the neighbor's raw intake ready lock; the
  stale request took a raw record and the column hung on the first call. Every lock of the core and memory tiles in
  the image's columns is now raised to its maximum (granting any such request while cores and tile DMAs are held in
  reset) before the lock initialization writes the real values. Shim locks are left alone (their DMA channels cannot
  be reset). Kernel behavior is otherwise unchanged.
diff --git a/loom/src/loom/target/arch/amd/xdna/aie2p/array/program.c b/loom/src/loom/target/arch/amd/xdna/aie2p/array/program.c
